## Command Discipline

- For simple repository requests such as listing the project root, checking Git status, reading files, or running workflow tests, use explicit PowerShell commands rooted at the project path.
- Do not run a bare `dir`, `ls`, `Get-ChildItem`, `git status`, or similar command until the shell location has been set to the project root.
- Never invent, simulate, summarize from memory, or use placeholder names for command output. Report filesystem listings only from actual command/tool results.
- If a command is pending user approval or has not run yet, say in Russian that the command is waiting for approval. Do not present any directory contents until the command completes.
- Never output placeholder entries such as `имя_папки_1`, `имя_папки_2`, `файл_1.txt`, or `файл_2.txt` as if they were real project files.
- When presenting filesystem names, append `\` to directory names and leave file names unchanged. For example: `Assets\`, `ProjectSettings\`, `.clinerules`.
- For "выведи список корневого каталога проекта", use:

```powershell
Set-Location -LiteralPath 'D:\PROJECTS\DarkTreeFPS2022\lfhrnhbagc2022'
Get-ChildItem -Force | Select-Object Mode, LastWriteTime, Length, @{Name='Name';Expression={ if ($_.PSIsContainer) { "$($_.Name)\" } else { $_.Name } }}
```

## AI Task Ownership

Use `docs\ai-tasks\` for durable agent handoffs. Task filenames must start with one of these owner prefixes:

- `CLINE-`: execute in this VS Code Cline chat.
- `CC-`: handoff for Claude Code in the terminal. In Cline, create or update the file, but do not execute it unless the user explicitly reassigns it to Cline.
- `CODEX-`: handoff for Codex. In Cline, create or update the file, but do not execute it unless the user explicitly reassigns it to Cline.

Every task file must include an `Owner:` line matching its filename prefix and a `Project:` line with `D:\PROJECTS\DarkTreeFPS2022\lfhrnhbagc2022`. If owner and filename disagree, or if `Status: needs-owner-review` is present, do not execute the task yet. Ask the user to confirm the owner or update the filename and `Owner:` together.

